<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C8.S1 — Iteration count and success probability</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C8.S1 — Sizing a Grover search</p></div><p>Let \(N=2^{ {@n@} }\) and let there be \(M={@M@}\) marked items. Write \(\theta=\arcsin\sqrt{M/N}\).</p><p>(a) Give the success probability after \(k\) iterations, as a function of <code>k</code> and <code>theta</code>.</p><p>\(p_k=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the leading-order optimal number of iterations (ignoring the floor), in terms of <code>N</code> and <code>M</code>.</p><p>\(k_{\mathrm{opt}}\approx\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) Evaluate that expression numerically for the values above (exact expression, no decimals).</p><p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(G\) rotates by \(2\theta\) in the good/bad plane starting at angle \(\theta\), so after \(k\) steps the good amplitude is \(\sin((2k+1)\theta)\) and \(p_k=\sin^{2}((2k+1)\theta)\).</p><p>(b) Solving \((2k+1)\theta=\pi/2\) gives \(k=\frac{\pi}{4\theta}-\frac12\); for \(M\ll N\), \(\theta\approx\sqrt{M/N}\) and \(k_{\mathrm{opt}}\approx\frac{\pi}{4}\sqrt{N/M}\).</p><p>(c) With \(N=2^{ {@n@} }\) and \(M={@M@}\): \(k\approx{@ta3@}\).</p><p>Note \(p_k\) is periodic in \(k\): running too long rotates past the target and lowers the success probability. This is why the number of iterations must be chosen in advance, and why unknown \(M\) requires the BBHT exponential schedule.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
